@startuml f8-task-finalization
title F8 - Task finalization (EX -> Router marks done, EX -> StateRegistry writes historical)

|AG|
start
:Agent loop complete;
:Emit final result with stdout and exit code;

|EX|
:Capture final stdout and exit code;

|EX|
:REST POST /tasks/:id/status to Router
 with status=terminal, result;

|Router|
:Mark task done in Router DB;
:slots_in_use = slots_in_use minus 1;

|EX|
:REST POST /events to State Registry
 with status=terminal, result (historical);

fork
  |Operator|
  :UI WS already shows final (subscribed via F3);

  |EX|
  :Stop container
   with SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after grace;
  :Unmount tmpfs (plaintext gone);

fork again
  |EX|
  :REST POST /executors/:id/ready to Router
 (signal available for next task);

  |Router|
:Mark executor as having at least one free slot;
:Router can now match a new pending task
 to this EX if slots_in_use is less than capacity;

end fork

note right
  Two concurrent paths from completion:
  1. EX marks the task done in Router (queue),
     Router decrements slots_in_use.
  2. EX writes the historical terminal event
     to State Registry (canonical record).
  These are independent writes; no broker.
end note

stop

@enduml